WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.410
It's snowing.

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:04.850
Hold out a dark glove and catch a few flakes.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.430
Now look closely at each one.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.790
Six arms.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.110
Six again.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.250
Each single crystal has six sides.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:22.510
In 1611 the astronomer Johannes Kepler wrote a little book asking why, and admitted that the science of his day couldn't answer him.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.440
So why does every snowflake have six sides?

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:34.090
In this mission, you'll start with a single molecule of water, and meet the two kinds of attraction that hold ice together.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.910
You'll find out how a snow crystal forms, and why Kepler's question took three centuries to answer.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: explain why every snowflake has six sides.
